<title>POLAND: Polish yr/yr CPI 19.1 pct in Nov vs 19.5 Oct.</title>
<headline>Polish yr/yr CPI 19.1 pct in Nov vs 19.5 Oct.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish consumer prices rose 1.3 percent in November against a 1.4 percent rise in October bringing year-on-year inflation down to 19.1 percent, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>CPI rose 17.1 percent in the January-November period, compared with a 19.8 percent rise in the corresponding period last year.  </p>
<p> POLISH CONSUMER PRICES    NOV 96    OCT 96	 NOV 95</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)    1.3	 1.4	     1.3</p>
<p> yr/yr change		   19.1	19.5	    22.0</p>
<p> services m/m change	   0.6	 1.6	     0.6</p>
<p> services yr/yr change	19.8	19.8	    21.9</p>
<p> food prices m/m change	2.2	 1.2	     1.8</p>
<p> food prices yr/yr change   19.3	19.9	    20.0</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
